WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.320
we have a voicemail number.

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:06.140
That number is two one nine two David Pakman.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:14.009
Here's a question that I don't know the implication
from the caller, but it's actually a really

00:00:14.009 --> 00:00:18.640
good question, which we talked about last
week on the show about what is safe in the

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.380
context of the virus.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.750
Take a listen.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:29.990
Hey, David, this is Christine from Louisiana,
right?

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:38.450
I was just wondering if I find this kind of
suspicious during this cove and I mean, all

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:43.480
these big, big box retailers have been allowed
to go almost full capacity at all times while

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.260
small businesses are reduced to, you know,
15 percent in California, 50 percent in other

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.260
places.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:51.060
Do you think that there is a connection?

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:58.500
Because all the money that comes to the, you
know, the Senate and the House and all the

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:03.980
politicians from these big box retailers and
that they have a vested interest in keeping

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.420
their stores open?

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:10.980
Listen, I don't know about the money piece,
but Scott Atlus recently brought this up.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:14.210
The radiologist that Trump had working for
him for a while.

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:21.280
He also said, why is it that a full capacity
big box store is safe and a small restaurant

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.670
at half capacity is not?

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:23.670
And you know what?

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.230
I agree with him.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:27.250
The thing is the conclusion may be different.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:30.350
I don't think the big box store at full capacity
is safe.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:35.130
And we have a report from El Paso, Texas,
which actually finds that a huge amount of

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:39.240
the contagion is happening in the big box
stores.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:44.830
Now, I don't know exactly what sort of mask
wearing requirements are enforced in El Paso,

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:46.330
Texas, in big box stores.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:50.270
And certainly the wearing of masks would reduce
the transmission.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:53.310
But this is a perfectly reasonable question,
except for me.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:59.360
The answer isn't open up restaurants at full
capacity, which are very, you know, smaller,

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:04.100
lower ceilings, less sophisticated ventilation
in many cases, et cetera.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:08.259
It's I don't think the full capacity big box
stores make any sense whatsoever.

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:11.529
So a very reasonable question, which I've
been asking as well.

00:02:11.529 --> 00:02:16.239
But I think we need to understand which side
is the answer we should be leaning towards.

